    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. regarding the bitumen part, do you think the viscosity loss is mostly due to the oxidative aging of the binder, or is it primarily just the sheer heat-induced softening during the peak summer months? i'm trying to figure out if we need to look at a different polymer-modified asphalt or if the subgrade just isn't stable enough.",
